---
import { withBase } from '../../core/site/base-path';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="About Valvia" description="Intended use, sources and limitations of Valvia.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About Valvia</h1>

    <h2 id="intended-use">Intended use</h2>
    <p>
      Valvia is a quick-reference aid for echocardiographers, cardiologists, fellows and sonographers. It displays
      reference ranges and cut-off values exactly as published in documents of the European Society of Cardiology
      (including the European Association of Cardiovascular Imaging) and the American Society of Echocardiography, each
      with its source and location in the document.
    </p>
    <p>
      Valvia is <strong>not a medical device</strong>. It does not calculate, interpret or classify measurements of
      individual patients, does not compute z-scores or risk scores, and does not give diagnostic or treatment advice.
      Clinical decisions remain the responsibility of the clinician.
    </p>

    <h2 id="disclaimer">Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Values are transcribed from the cited documents and may contain errors. Always verify a value against the original
      guideline before clinical use. Content marked <strong>"Not yet clinically reviewed"</strong> is a draft that has
      not been checked by a clinical expert.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
    <p>
      Only ESC (including EACVI) and ASE documents are used, plus paediatric z-score datasets that one of these
      documents cites. Algorithms and figures are linked to the source, never redrawn. Each value shows its society,
      document, year and table, figure, section or page.
    </p>

    <h2 id="how-values-are-shown">How values are shown</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Lengths in mm, areas in cm², blood-flow velocities in m/s, tissue Doppler velocities in cm/s. Tap a converted
        value to see it as published.
      </li>
      <li>CT and CMR values carry a badge; all other values are echocardiographic.</li>
      <li>When current documents disagree, both values are shown; Valvia never picks one.</li>
      <li>Values from superseded documents appear under "Previous recommendations".</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="report">Report a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If a value looks wrong, please report it with the page and the source location:
      <a href="https://github.com/tudorgrigoriu90/valvia/issues/new" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
        open an issue on GitHub<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href={withBase(base, '/')}>Back to the home page</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
